    "summary": "Fiery The Other One jam and solid playing despite wobble",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a standout performance of The Other One, with Jerry’s soaring leads and Bill’s tight drumming. Jack Straw and One More Saturday Night also shine, making this a strong late‑1971 outing even though the soundboard has noticeable wobble.",
    "review": "October 26, 1971 at the Palestra finds the Dead in fine form, rolling through a two‑set setlist that balances tight songwriting with an adventurous second‑set excursion. Jerry Garcia’s guitar is especially inspired on The Other One and El Paso, where he adds a pedal‑steel cameo and a flurry of fills that lift the jam into fiery territory. Bill Kreutzmann provides a punchy, more assertive drum foundation than many shows from this year, while early Keith Godchaux slots in barrel‑housing organ tones that give the music extra depth. The first set moves smoothly through classics like Jack Straw and One More Saturday Night, and the second set caps off with an energetic transition from Truckin' into a soaring The Other One before a brief Johnny B. Goode finale. Though the available soundboard source suffers from wobble, pitch flutter and occasional dropouts, it remains the most complete document of this performance and captures enough of the band’s chemistry to make it worthwhile for Deadheads seeking a solid 1971 snapshot.",
